## Summary

**Reproduced.** The finding holds on `main` (`ee528e1`): `rb test` reported *22 tests, 21 passed, 0 failed* while asserting nothing. Two causes — the three `.rb` files shipped with all 21 `test` blocks inside `//` comments, and `TestHarness::run_source` only recognised the `// test "…"` marker convention and fed the *commented* body lines to the lexer, where they lex to an empty program and report a **pass**.

**Red first.** `tests/redblue_suite_test.rs` (8 `#[test]`) was written and run before any production change: **0 passed, 8 failed**, with `edge_suite_reports_at_least_40_redblue_tests` reporting `found 22`.

**Smallest change that greens it.** One production file, `src/testing/harness.rs`: discover real `test "…" ... end` blocks from the parser (so block boundaries are exact, not line-scanned) and run each body on its own analysed `Vm`. `report_test` extracted so both discovery paths share one outcome path. The `// test` marker convention is preserved for `tests/discovery_test.rs` / `tests/expect_test.rs`.

**Suite.** 187 assertion-bearing blocks across 10 files (was 22, all vacuous), 57 named `edge_*`, 24 using `try`/`catch` to assert a failure is produced, 0 skipped.

**Gates.**

| Gate | Result |
|---|---|
| `cargo fmt --all -- --check` | pass |
| `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` | pass |
| `cargo test` | 67 passed, 0 failed |
| `rb test` | 187 run / 187 passed / 0 failed, exit 0 |
| `./rbops/verify.sh phase-003` | **could not run — `rbops/` does not exist in this checkout** |

That last row is the honest gap: the RBOPS tree is not in this repository, so I did not run, inspect, or substitute for it. `.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs exactly `cargo build`, `cargo test`, `cargo clippy -- -D warnings` — all verified green locally. If `verify.sh` enforces more, this phase is unverified against it.

**Also found, not fixed** (`phases/phase-003/FINDINGS.md`, 13 items, all `file:line`-anchored with reproductions): the entire stdlib is dead (`stdlib::builtin_function` is never called — ~35 functions raise `Unknown function`), `{interp}` is never substituted though AGENTS §2 lists it as an invariant, `Value::Function` stores no body so every user function returns `nothing`, `break`/`skip` are ignored by all loops, `has`/`new` have no parser rule, `constant` is unparsed so `modules/MathUtils.rb` cannot run (pre-existing, reproduced on stashed `main`), the lexer has no `<`/`>`/`==` while the formatter emits `is greater than` that the parser rejects, and two of the three assertion forms AGENTS §3.1 permits do not exist. One matrix row — infinite-loop guard — has **zero** coverage, because `while` is uncapped and `break` is ignored; it is recorded as a finding rather than papered over.

